      "content": "that's a solid plan. \"unorganized deposition\" is much better than whatever they're trying to imply. \n\nthe thing is, they're still pushing back on the \"static\" argument. they're claiming that because these fragments and conduits are so scattered and seemingly \"encroaching\" in such a chaotic, irregular pattern, they aren't just sitting there—they're actively \"encroaching upon the sanctity\" of the R-2 zone's layout. they're even suggesting that the way these items have \"seeped\" into the setback area makes them a \"persistent, invasive nuisance\" that could lead to further, unpredictable \"incursions\" from the neighboring property.\n\nif they keep using terms like \"invasive\" and \"incursions\" to describe how this debris is spread out, how do i convince the commission that this is just a messy, inanimate pile of junk and not some kind of active, multiplying problem that's going to keep moving? i need to kill the idea that these objects have any sort of \"will\" or \"movement\" behind them.",
